{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity","id":1385598,"title":"25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade's Fall of London review or \"Positive Negativity\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T06:27:39-07:00","id":1385598,"title":"25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade's Fall of London review or \"Positive Negativity\"","content":"<a href=\"https://utilitymuffinlabs.com/25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade/\" target=\"_blank\">https://utilitymuffinlabs.com/25-yea...he-masquerade/</a><br /> <br /> The good people at Utility Muffin Labs just did their review of THE FALL OF LONDON, which I felt was worth sharing because it's a 2 hour podcast review of said Chronicle. I absolutely love Nathan and Bob's commentary as I am a regular listener of their reviews. Sometimes I agree with them and sometimes I don't. However, I'm going to bring attention to this review in particular because I think a lot of people would enjoy it. It's also an example of what I consider to be &quot;positive negativity&quot; which is to say that they generally tear into this book but in a way that I feel creates discussion rather than shuts it down. I feel there's a lack of examples of healthy criticism around there and this really takes the cake for it.<br /> <br /> Some highlights:<br /> <br /> + The pair of them discuss the continuity issues they have with Mithras' portrayal as well as relationships to canon characters. How he's now Roger de Camden's lover while barely touching on the fact Queen Anne was his lover [perfectly possible for a vampire, IMHO]. Also, how he is no longer sharing a body with Monty Coven but planning on throwing him out.<br /> <br /> + They also talk about how V5 sometimes feels like it is a different continuity from the V20 books [which I disagree with] but that isn't necessarily a bad thing because it is an introduction for a lot of people who don't need to be buying 125 books versus 5.<br /> <br /> + Their talk about how the Second Inquisition doesn't make sense to them in this book while discussing all the various ways it COULD have made sense if it had been done differently. Also, making fun of the fact that they're equipped with stuff directly taken from Blade.<br /> <br /> + The book's poor handling of the Sabbat and how the sect is being treated as a bunch of one-dimensional wild monsters versus an arcane sect of occultists.<br /> <br /> + How the PCs are often expected to fight people who would utterly wreck them not just by stats but by age.<br /> <br /> + They also proceed to discuss the elements of the book that they really enjoyed from the artwork, certain characters, and it's toolbox approach to storytelling.<br /> <br /> I definitely think its worth a listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:21:32-07:00","id":1385654,"title":"","content":"I'll definitely give it a listen!<br /> <br /> Viewing V5 as an alternate timeline to cherry pick from seems like a useful recommendation for many of us. I even think it's validated by the retconning of the Tal'mahe'ra in the Revised Edition of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T17:28:46-07:00","id":1385691,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on their review where I agree and disagree with them:<br /> <br /> <b>Agreement</b><br /> <br /> + I think the Arcanum is totally 100% the Watchers from Highlander. Well, I also think they're the Talamasca but I think that those are the inspirations for the Watchers.<br /> <br /> + I definitely think that the weapons of the Second Inquisition are silly and Blade inspired. They really needed to be creations of the Arcanum using Technomancy or made with an illusion to the Technocracy to make any sort of sense. UV lights and anti-coalagulates should do nothing to vampires.<br /> <br /> + I agree that the flashbacks do nothing for the game and are very distracting. They should really ditch them.<br /> <br /> + The London Underground section of the book is probably one of the best parts of it. Also, it works primarily as a toolbox for gaming rather than something that is a straight Chronicle.<br /> <br /> + The Sabbat in the gamebook are a bunch of stereotypes that are an afterthought at best.<br /> <br /> + Not sure why Queen Anne wants to kill her sire NOW of all times. Also, why the PCs are expected to be able to pull it off.<br /> <br /> + Regina Blake is the best pony of all the characters inside.<br /> <br /> + The art is gorgeous.<br /> <br /> <b>Disagreement</b><br /> <br /> + I think Bob was just DEAD WRONG about the idea that vampires wouldn't engage in dialberie. He said that age should be the primary determination of vampire power and that most vampires would be willing to wait. People in real life are not patient and dialberie adds a HUGE amount to the game. Amusingly, he makes repeated references to the Highlander TV show but doesn't draw any comparisons to the Quickening.<br /> <br /> + I think they were overly nitpicky about the idea of creating a ritual that would empower Mithras back to 4th generation. In fact, I don't get the impression they actually understand why Mithras would want to be back to 4th generation or rid himself of Monty Coven's soul battling for control. I mean, it's a somewhat silly ritual but it works just fine for motivations. Voldemort wants to get his power back to full percent.<br /> <br /> + Weirdly, I think their belief that this feels off from Revised is wrong because Operation:Antigen is one big continuity homage. There's the Arcanum, Knights of Saint George, and other things that are all very obscure lore dumps. They also mention the 2nd Inquisition is an umbrella term for a bunch of groups doing their thing seperately, which this is exactly such.<br /> <br /> <b>My own thoughts</b><br /> <br /> + The Anarchs got shafted in this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:46:26-07:00","id":1385728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385691#post1385691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ The Anarchs got shafted in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...... especially with no Vaseline....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T22:18:59-07:00","id":1385746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385728#post1385728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah...... especially with no Vaseline....</div> </div> </div> </div>The City of Punk with no Anarch characters!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:14:59-07:00","id":1385753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385691#post1385691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+ Regina Blake is the best pony of all the characters inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. She was the best character presented in this. I just wish she had stats in V20 format.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:12:24-07:00","id":1385791,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with your assessment of their style of criticism and most of your points.<br /> <br /> I also love that podcast! <br /> <br /> + overall the book is good and I enjoyed it<br /> <br /> - The ritual feels too much like a plot device (which it is and that is fine) and not like a natural part of the setting<br /> - I would change that de Camden developed it specifically for Mithras situation (with lots of effort) based on necromancy (Oblivion) to in effect restore his master/lover. <br /> <br /> - Something about the Inquisition seems of to me, but I can't put my finger on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:19:26-07:00","id":1385793,"title":"","content":"I think Mithras is bi, but he mostly prefers girls. Him and Kemintiri had a thing too.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t see any continuity issues<br /> <br /> I really liked their portrayal of the Knights of St. George<br /> <br /> I agree about the Sabbat and I wish they had more Anarch stuff<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2582_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2582\" data-vbnamecard=\"2582\">Gangrel44</a> ewwwwww, but still funny \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> What\u2019s a pony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T06:53:37-07:00","id":1385810,"title":"","content":"I've never really had an issue with the idea of vampires' tastes in romantic partners expanding as they get older. As a vampire's humanity lowers, they start to lose the ability to engage in actual sex and need the Blush of Life to simulate sex. And I think a part of that is a gradual lessening of sexual libido. To borrow the modern verbiage, I think elder vampires, when they do take lovers, are &quot;romantic asexuals.&quot;<br /> <br /> So no, I don't think Mithras and Roger de Camden are banging like two college guys who have just realized they like men. But two immortal beings who have realized they enjoy each other's company, are intellectually equal and emotionally compatible, and have decided that they want to make each other's nights a bit less lonely? Yeah, I can totally see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:48:47-07:00","id":1385833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385691#post1385691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts on their review where I agree and disagree with them:<br /> <br /> + I think the Arcanum is totally 100% the Watchers from Highlander. Well, I also think they're the Talamasca but I think that those are the inspirations for the Watchers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well since in my setting the Watchers and immortals are a part of my setting they <i>are </i>the Arcanum if I ever got around to introducing either into my game. Thus far its remained background lore that has yet to come up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T08:22:05-07:00","id":1385840,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> makes sense. Course, he was much younger when he met Kemintiri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:30:11-07:00","id":1385916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385793#post1385793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mithras is bi, but he mostly prefers girls. Him and Kemintiri had a thing too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view of vampires and sex is the fact that sex is blood and blood is sex. Mithras is old enough that he almost certainly feeds almost exclusively on Kindred blood or his long torpors are designed to prevent just that. Either way, any vampire that he feeds on and doesn't kill is someone that he is showing great emotional attachment. As a cult leader, I tend to imagine he's &quot;lovers&quot; with many of his priests and priestesses as a way of showing both their submission and his favor. At Presence 9 it's a religious experience too.<br /> <br /> Mithras would worry about Roger dying as much because he's an incredibly useful pawn and servant than any lingering emotional attachment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree about the Sabbat and I wish they had more Anarch stuff </div> </div> </div>The title is a Clash song after all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385791#post1385791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;12002&quot;]- The ritual feels too much like a plot device (which it is and that is fine) and not like a natural part of the setting. I would change that de Camden developed it specifically for Mithras situation (with lots of effort) based on necromancy (Oblivion) to in effect restore his master/lover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it makes more sense for the ritual to have been developed to restore Mithras' power and remove Monty Coven's soul because the ritual as designed historically seems like a &quot;Magic Jar&quot; spell from D&amp;D and that's the opposite of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Something about the Inquisition seems of to me, but I can't put my finger on it. </div> </div> </div>One thing that isn't really a retcon or not is the fact that this could easily be a self-contained plotline completely devoid of the larger V5 world. This is a campaign you could do for V20 and all you have to do is substitute that Mithras has a plan to sweep up the Masquerade violations afterward. Like, after Mithras either leaves London or is killed, his cult eliminates all of the Antigen agents by having his sleeper agents summon them to a tube station that has a bomb present and then his hackers wipe clean their databases while government officials [under his control] clean out everything.<br /> <br /> This is easily a V20 chronicle that way because, yes, Mithras [or even the Camarilla's Justicars] are that smart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-05-2020, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:13:22-07:00","id":1385935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I like the idea that this could be a self-contained plot line and that Mithras plans to simply eliminate Operation Antigen after he regains his full power. I\u2019ve only read the first two chapters so far, but I\u2019m gonna read some more later on tonight.<br /> <br /> Also, in my head canon I made Chuck Bass from Gossip Girl a priest of the Cult of Mithras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:24:24-07:00","id":1385967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385935#post1385935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> in my head canon I made Chuck Bass from Gossip Girl a priest of the Cult of Mithras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me Jenny Humphrey any day.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T18:41:35-07:00","id":1385989,"title":"","content":"My friend kinda looks like her a little. But I thought of Chuck because his family has Wall Street connections and the Bull of Wall Street is also literally the Bull of Mithras (that\u2019s where the phrase \u201cbull market\u201d comes from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T19:05:15-07:00","id":1385990,"title":"","content":"Some interesting things they touched on in the podcast that are worth discussing:<br /> <br /> + This is another case of retconning the timeline and one of the first retcons of V5. As they mentioned, THE CAMARILLA book established that the London police tracked down and decapitated Queen Anne Bowesley. This establishes that Queen Anne is alive and well, at least until your player characters choose to kill her or not. This is a small retcon but it is a significant one that shows them putting plot before continuity.<br /> <br /> + Another retcon is the fact Mithras is differently characterized in his relationship to Monty Coven in BJD. Mithras in this chronicle wants to restore himself to full power and get rid of Monty's soul, which seems a reasonable assumption to me. However, BJD had Mithras quite happy to be sharing a soul with Monty Coven as it has reinvigorated his love of life and reality. They were happily joined together in BJD but now active enemies here.<br /> <br /> + I really do think this is a kind of self-contained Chronicle that can be run more or less without any of V5's changes. It's based around the idea of Mithras making a pass at the control of London again and while his actions of KILLING EVERYONE may be extreme, I'd hardly say it's extreme for a man over 6000 years old. I do believe it's within his power to shut down Operation: Antigen<br /> after he's made use of it and probably the Camarilla too if it's independent of the other V5 disasters.<br /> <br /> + I actually think this book functions as a makeshift LONDON BY NIGHT and it's kind of interesting they chose to do it as a Chronicle versus a City Book. Do Chronicles really sell better than City Books? Still, it's entirely possible to use the book to run campaigns in London prior to Mithras' revenge.<br /> <br /> + They're reviewing THE CHICAGO FOLIOS next and I'm very excited about that. I'm also pleased that LET THE STREETS RUN RED entered layout yesterday so it's possible we'll be able to see it reviewed soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:02:32-07:00","id":1386054,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I\u2019m gonna read Chapter 4 of Fall of London tonight. Can\u2019t wait \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:51:01-07:00","id":1386133,"title":"","content":"Finished the podcast and had some thoughts as well.<br /> <br /> First as an aside I remembered why I stopped listening to their podcasts in the first place. That being Bob's non sequitur tangents and holier than thou one right way approach to roleplaying. Nate makes the podcast for me but I digress.<br /> <br /> The podcast does however serve its purpose as a consumer wanting to know if a book is worth spending my cash on. I can say I wont buy the book but I dont think I was ever going to as its not a product Im in the market for. I was however interested in the lore of the book and how the SI was being portrayed as the main threat of 5th edition to this point. My take from their review is that they've been beefed up to a comic book style level with Reed Richards level tech that puts them on part with Kindred. Im wondering however since it keep getting the impression that the power level of the SI is fluctuating wildly from book to book.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of the ritual to return Mithras to his body is interesting however I really liked where they were heading with him in BJD as I really liked the Mithras/Monty merging and was interested to see where they were going with that. Now I have the answer as no where and we're going to have Mithras back as a fixture in 5th edition moving forward. Just a missed opportunity for me personally.<br /> <br /> I'll also echo what others have said about the Sabbat. White Wolf needs to address this sooner rather than laters as its a big black eye on 5th edition.<br /> <br /> Finally I also disagree with Bob's take on diablerie. In a game all about power hungry fiends and a society where advancement is often a carrot that is dangled to make the neonates and ancillae think they have bigger and better nights ahead its really a lie and one the elders continually perpetuate. How many stories have been born out of diablerie and how much more bland would VTM be without that facet of the game. I think it would be much much worse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:07:40-07:00","id":1386141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1386054#post1386054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I\u2019m gonna read Chapter 4 of Fall of London tonight. Can\u2019t wait \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't wait for your thoughts once done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:12:57-07:00","id":1386157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1386133#post1386133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished the podcast and had some thoughts as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for participating!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First as an aside I remembered why I stopped listening to their podcasts in the first place. That being Bob's non sequitur tangents and holier than thou one right way approach to roleplaying. Nate makes the podcast for me but I digress. </div> </div> </div>I admit I dislike the fact they are so hard on Anarchs and so pro-Sabbat, but I think you need both to play off one another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The podcast does however serve its purpose as a consumer wanting to know if a book is worth spending my cash on. I can say I wont buy the book but I dont think I was ever going to as its not a product Im in the market for. I was however interested in the lore of the book and how the SI was being portrayed as the main threat of 5th edition to this point. My take from their review is that they've been beefed up to a comic book style level with Reed Richards level tech that puts them on part with Kindred. Im wondering however since it keep getting the impression that the power level of the SI is fluctuating wildly from book to book. </div> </div> </div>I confess, I was pleased they did acknowledge the poor editing of the book. I usually ignore this as all books are going to have SOME typos and grammatical mistakes, even after editing, but this was especially egregious. I also think they were pretty fair to the book even if I disagreed with some of their complaints. They listed what they liked and listed what they disliked in roughly equal measure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the idea of the ritual to return Mithras to his body is interesting however I really liked where they were heading with him in BJD as I really liked the Mithras/Monty merging and was interested to see where they were going with that. Now I have the answer as no where and we're going to have Mithras back as a fixture in 5th edition moving forward. Just a missed opportunity for me personally. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was a big reversal on that. I admit, I always felt Mithras would want to get back his original power level, though, despite BJD saying otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll also echo what others have said about the Sabbat. White Wolf needs to address this sooner rather than laters as its a big black eye on 5th edition. </div> </div> </div>It's hilarious that the most we know about the Sabbat is the two paragraphs in THE CHICAGO FOLIOS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally I also disagree with Bob's take on diablerie. In a game all about power hungry fiends and a society where advancement is often a carrot that is dangled to make the neonates and ancillae think they have bigger and better nights ahead its really a lie and one the elders continually perpetuate. How many stories have been born out of diablerie and how much more bland would VTM be without that facet of the game. I think it would be much much worse. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm genuinely confused why he doesn't think vampires would be murdering each other left and right for a leg up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:33:20-07:00","id":1386186,"title":"","content":"It might be the games multiple writers causing the confusion. I have read books where diablerie is the unforgivable sin going back to the early days, black streaks in your aura getting a blood hunt called on you. Then they have D&amp;D type adventures where it's the stated goal in the title, or novels where it has no consequence. I think Diablerie changed over time to a more accepted practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:34:27-07:00","id":1386187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1386186#post1386186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be the games multiple writers causing the confusion. I have read books where diablerie is the unforgivable sin going back to the early days, black streaks in your aura getting a blood hunt called on you. Then they have D&amp;D type adventures where it's the stated goal in the title, or novels where it has no consequence. I think Diablerie changed over time to a more accepted practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a particularly unaccepted practice dating back to 1st Edition. After all, diablerie is the point of the Blood Hunt.<br /> <br /> One of the most common methods of execution in the Camarilla makes it legal to eat a fellow Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:59:52-07:00","id":1386271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1386187#post1386187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a particularly unaccepted practice dating back to 1st Edition. After all, diablerie is the point of the Blood Hunt.<br /> <br /> One of the most common methods of execution in the Camarilla makes it legal to eat a fellow Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. Only during a Blood Hunt, or a Sabbat Incursion was Diablerie legal in the Camarilla....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:47:49-07:00","id":1386997,"title":"","content":"Depressing to see V5 continues to throw out much more interesting plot hooks from BJD for the sake of tired old tropes. (More power)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:18:39-07:00","id":1387007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385598-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-fall-of-london-review-or-positive-negativity?p=1385990#post1385990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> + Another retcon is the fact Mithras is differently characterized in his relationship to Monty Coven in BJD. Mithras in this chronicle wants to restore himself to full power and get rid of Monty's soul, which seems a reasonable assumption to me. However, BJD had Mithras quite happy to be sharing a soul with Monty Coven as it has reinvigorated his love of life and reality. They were happily joined together in BJD but now active enemies here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That may not be a retcon so much as a typical example of a vampire becoming infatuated with someone and then losing interest after the honeymoon. Usually this results in them embracing them, treating them amazingly for a while, then reducing them in status from the love of their unlife, to just another pawn to be used up and abandoned. However, this is a unique case in which the youngster is his own diablerist instead of some mortal he became obsessed with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:56:24-07:00","id":1387598,"title":"","content":"I loved Fall of London overall. The different chapters were all interesting and flowed together really well, and each of several possible endings is thoroughly explored. My only objection is that it\u2019s too dependent on the use of pregenerated characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:57:04-07:00","id":1387599,"title":"","content":"I also liked how detailed the NPC writeups were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}